-- title:
--   Order one at a centred place for a height-one uniformiser
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and a finite extension $K'/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $C' =$ `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K'` for the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ consisting of those elements of the subfield `fieldOver (1 * q) K'` generated by the constant series from $K'$ together with $j$ and $j_{q}$ (the series `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) that are integral over the subring generated by the constant series from `coeffSubring A K'` together with $j$. Let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime ideal of $C'$ of height $1$ with $q \notin \mathfrak{p}$, and let $r \in \mathfrak{p}$, $r \neq 0$, be such that the localisation $C'_{\mathfrak{p}}$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $r$, this image having `addVal` equal to $1$. Let $W$ be a place of the field `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a proper valuation subring containing the constants and a principal ideal ring — and assume that for every $g$ in that field whose Laurent series lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K'`, membership of $g$ in $W$'s valuation subring is equivalent to $g \cdot s_0 = r_0$ for some $r_0, s_0 \in C'$ with $s_0 \notin \mathfrak{p}$. Then for any element $gr$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` whose underlying Laurent series equals that of $r$, one has $W.\mathrm{ord}(gr) = 1$, the order being minus the logarithm of the value of $gr$ under the adic valuation attached to $W$.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness statement for a place centred at a height-one prime away from $q$: the valuation ring of $W$ meeting the functions with expansions in $K'(j, j_q)$ exactly in $C'_{\mathfrak{p}}$ forces a uniformiser of $\mathfrak{p}$ to remain a uniformiser at $W$, because passing from $K'$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a constant-field extension in characteristic zero. It is used in the local analysis of the nodes of the modular curve of level $q$, in the computations of the order of a coordinate at places centred at $j = 0$ and $j = 1728$ in a crossing presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_ord_generator_eq_one_of_heightOne_of_ringIff.lean

